From: rtw89-usb-ap-fix <local@patch>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 10:31:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtw89: do not redefine ieee80211_get_sn in OpenWrt backports

OpenWrt 24.10 builds mac80211 from a 6.12 backports tree while the
target kernel is 6.6.119. Upstream rtw89 adds an ieee80211_get_sn()
compat helper for kernels older than 6.9, but the backports mac80211
headers already provide it.

Guard the helper out when CPTCFG_VERSION is defined so the same source
can build against OpenWrt backports without a duplicate static inline.
---
diff --git a/core.h b/core.h
--- a/core.h
+++ b/core.h
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ struct rtw89_regd_data;
 
 extern const struct ieee80211_ops rtw89_ops;
 
-#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 9, 0)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 9, 0) && !defined(CPTCFG_VERSION)
 static inline u16 ieee80211_get_sn(struct ieee80211_hdr *hdr)
 {
 	return le16_get_bits(hdr->seq_ctrl, IEEE80211_SCTL_SEQ);
